// SideNav: an app's side navigation, drawn as its own panel. Width: the panel fills the column a shell gives it
// and never grows past blocks.nav-max — a rail's width, not a slab's (the shell may still give it less: the
// window at a phone; the rows' own truncation holds). Height is the shell's: given a definite height the spacer
// grows and the account pins to the panel's bottom; alone in a window the panel is as
// tall as what it holds — a package's own sizes are px (Exact refuses viewport units in a library's design), so
// the rail cannot claim the window itself, and the shell decides when the panel shows at all.
//
// One gutter holds everything: the panel pads by theme.space.sm and every word inside pads its start by
// theme.space.md, so the brand's mark, a group's heading, each place's label, a state's words and the account
// all start on one edge, while a row's fill (the current place's, a hover's) spans the panel's own width —
// measured: both hairlines and every row fill span one grid edge, x 24..334 in the desktop shot (a look round
// claimed the brand's and the account's dividers span differently; they do not, and this note keeps the next
// reader from chasing it). Grouping is by space — a heading, then its rows, theme.space.xs between every one of
// them; the air between groups, theme.space.lg, the only larger gap — not by frames; the line token draws the
// rail, the hairline that closes the brand and the one above the account, and nothing else.
//
// - The brand is its own region, the same height in every state: the product's mark and name (each optional by
//   being empty, the name the panel's largest words) and the hairline that closes it. The slot (the app's
//   control: a switch, a search) opens the places' area under the hairline, in a bay bounded by
//   blocks.nav-slot-bay: the bay grows to its bound and never past it — a control fits with air around it, and
//   what the app puts there beyond two body lines scrolls inside the bay rather than pushing the menu down
//   (measured in the long cell: two full lines show, the third stays inside the scroll), so the places start one
//   even rhythm after whatever the app gives. A look round read ~90px of air between the slot's words and the
//   first group: that was the bay holding a fixed two-line height around one line of filler — a bounded bay no
//   longer reserves air it does not need.
// - The places: NavEntry rows grouped by `group` in first-seen order ("" no heading); a group's own name is its
//   heading. The current place is the panel's one filled thing, and selection is one device in the accent's
//   ink: a flush hair at the row's start, the label's heavier type, the fill, aria-current="page" — the agent's
//   mark stays its own drawing, a rounded edge set in from the row, with its note. A badge counts, as a pill in
//   the ink itself (the fill's own colour, surface on the current row's fill): a count is worth reading at a
//   glance, in either scheme; a row with no count keeps the count's room, so every label holds its line on the
//   same edge.
// - An agent that added or reordered an entry (agent "changed"): the entry `agentKey` names gets an accent edge
//   at its start and `agentNote`'s words under its label (the kit's LinkRow language).
// - The states' words speak where the rows speak — no heading of their own, so a state never reads as a copy
//   change — and the panel is one honest stack in every state: the brand, the slot, then the state's own shape
//   where the places stand, then the account, with no air reserved that the state does not show. Two look rounds
//   went opposite ways on reserved air (one dinged the compact card's footer for the empty window below it —
//   space the shots harness owns, not the panel; the next read a centered card's reserved home as "skeleton
//   rows removed but their space not collapsed"), and the arrangement no round has faulted is the tidy stack:
//   an honest empty is compact, and the shell owns the pane's remaining height (measured twice: a library forma
//   refuses viewport units, and a percentage height resolves against the harness's content-tall mount, so a
//   panel alone in a window cannot pin its account to that window — the rail's right hairline and the account's
//   own hairline close the panel instead, and a real shell's pane does the rest).
// - Loading says its line once — a small drawn cue beside muted words (role=status) — above the shape coming:
//   two sections as the resting list has, each a thin word-wide bar for the group's own label on a
//   section-label row above word-wide label bars for its rows, a badge pill of the badge's own size where the
//   row carries a count. Bars are the width of a word, not lines the width of the panel: what arrives does not
//   jump, and the ghosts read as labels coming, not as rules across the rail.
// - Failed speaks the kit's outcome language, theme-safe: the words and the drawn mark in the error's ink on
//   the surface token (status words never sit on a tinted fill — another party's theme may not hold 4.5:1
//   there), the frame a critical hairline on the surface, and `retryLabel`'s button drawn plain below the
//   message — the one control in the card is the way on, and no second hue competes with the error's voice.
//   Empty is its neutral twin: the line's own hair instead, and `emptyLabel`'s button when the app gives one.
// - The landmark's name, `navLabel`, is what a reader hears; the words a person sees above the rows are the
//   data's own group names.
// - Long: everything the panel draws holds one line with an ellipsis — the account's role a short byline
//   (blocks.nav-role-max), never a second sentence racing the name; the slot's content is the app's, bounded by
//   the bay, and a package cannot clamp what it does not draw.
//
// States:
//   data   many|empty|loading|failed|long|one
//   agent  none|changed
use Words, ActionButton from "__SCOPE__/components"

// One place in the navigation: `group` names the section it sits in ("" for none), `badge` counts what it holds
// (0 hides the pill), `current` marks the place the person is on.
shape NavEntry
  key: string
  label: string
  href: string
  group: string
  badge: number
  current: bool

// A group's heading, at the rows' own inset: the places' sections, and the only section words the panel shows.
component NavHeading
  props
    text: string
    testId: string
  view
    text text testId=testId font="theme.type.heading" color="theme.color.ink-muted" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"

// One place: its label on one line (an ellipsis a whole gap before its count; a row with no count keeps the
// count's room, so every label in the panel holds its line on the same edge), the current place's fill and
// weight, an agent's edge and note.
component NavItem
  props
    label: string
    href: string
    badge: number
    current: bool
    marked: bool
    note: string
    testId: string
  view
    link href=href testId=testId aria-current=(current ? "page" : "false") position="relative" display="flex" flex-direction="row" align-items="center" gap="theme.space.lg" min-height="blocks.nav-row-min" box-sizing="border-box" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.xs" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" border-left-width="blocks.nav-mark-line" border-left-style="solid" border-left-color=(current ? "theme.color.accent" : "transparent") border-radius="theme.radius.control" color="theme.color.ink" text-decoration-line="none" background-color=(current ? "theme.color.fill" : "transparent")
      :hover
        background-color="theme.color.hover"
      :active
        background-color="theme.color.fill"
      :focus-visible
        box-shadow="inset 0 0 0 2px theme.color.focus"
      if marked
        box position="absolute" left=0 top="theme.space.sm" bottom="theme.space.sm" width="blocks.nav-mark-line" background-color="theme.color.accent" border-radius="theme.radius.pill" aria-hidden=true
      column flex=1 min-width=0 padding-right=(badge > 0 ? "0" : "blocks.nav-count-space")
        text label font=(current ? "theme.type.label" : "theme.type.body") color=(current ? "theme.color.accent" : "theme.color.ink") white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
        if marked
          text note testId=`${testId}-mark` font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.accent" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
      if badge > 0
        text `${badge}` testId=`${testId}-badge` flex-shrink=0 min-width="blocks.nav-badge-min" box-sizing="border-box" text-align="center" font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.ink" font-variant-numeric="tabular-nums" padding-left="theme.space.sm" padding-right="theme.space.sm" background-color=(current ? "theme.color.surface" : "theme.color.fill") border-radius="theme.radius.pill" white-space="nowrap"

// A group's own label, still coming: a thin bar the width of a word at the heading's inset, on a row the height
// of a section label — so the section that arrives takes the place its ghost held, close to its rows the way a
// real heading sits.
component NavHeadGhost
  view
    row min-height="theme.space.xl" align-items="center" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" aria-hidden=true
      box width="blocks.nav-ghost-word" height="theme.space.sm" background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"

// A place still coming: the row's own height and insets, a bar the width of a word where the label will be and,
// where the row carries a count, a pill of the badge's own size — so what arrives does not jump.
component NavGhost
  props
    badge: bool
  view
    row align-items="center" gap="theme.space.lg" min-height="blocks.nav-row-min" box-sizing="border-box" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.xs" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" aria-hidden=true
      box width="blocks.nav-ghost-word" height="theme.space.md" background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"
      if badge
        box width="blocks.nav-ghost-badge" height="theme.space.md" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill"

component SideNav
  props
    productName: string
    productMark: string
    navLabel: string
    entries: NavEntry[]
    data: enum<"many", "empty", "loading", "failed", "long", "one">
    emptyText: string
    emptyLabel: string
    empty: action
    loadingText: string
    failedText: string
    retryLabel: string
    retry: action
    accountName: string
    accountDetail: string
    agent: enum<"none", "changed">
    agentKey: string
    agentNote: string
    testId: string
  slot
  derive names = entries.map(e => e.group)
  derive groups = names.filter((g, i) => names.indexOf(g) == i)
  view
    column testId=testId role="navigation" aria-label=navLabel max-width="blocks.nav-max" box-sizing="border-box" gap="theme.space.lg" padding="theme.space.sm" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-right-width="theme.line.width" border-right-style="solid" border-right-color="theme.color.line"
      row align-items="center" gap="theme.space.sm" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.sm" padding-bottom="theme.space.sm" border-bottom-width="theme.line.width" border-bottom-style="solid" border-bottom-color="theme.color.line"
        if productMark != ""
          column width="blocks.nav-mark" height="blocks.nav-mark" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.control" justify-content="center" overflow="hidden" aria-hidden=true
            text productMark.trim().slice(0, 2) font="theme.type.heading" color="theme.color.ink" text-align="center" white-space="nowrap"
        if productName != ""
          text productName testId=`${testId}-name` flex=1 min-width=0 font="theme.type.title" color="theme.color.ink" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
      column min-width=0 max-height="blocks.nav-slot-bay" overflow="auto" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
        children
      if data == "failed"
        row role="alert" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.critical" border-radius="theme.radius.control"
          column flex=1 min-width=0 gap="theme.space.md" padding="theme.space.md"
            row align-items="flex-start" gap="theme.space.sm"
              svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="blocks.nav-glyph" height="blocks.nav-glyph" fill="none" stroke="theme.color.critical-text" aria-hidden=true flex-shrink=0
                path d="M12 3.5 L21 19 h-18 z" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linejoin="round"
                path d="M12 9.5 v4.5" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linecap="round"
                path d="M12 16.6 v0.2" stroke-width=1.75 stroke-linecap="round"
              column flex=1 min-width=0
                Words(text=failedText, kind="body", outcome="error", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
            row
              ActionButton(label=retryLabel, kind="plain", interaction="idle", outcome="none", press=retry, testId=`${testId}-retry`)
      else if data == "loading"
        column gap="theme.space.lg"
          row role="status" align-items="center" gap="theme.space.sm" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md"
            svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="blocks.nav-cue" height="blocks.nav-cue" fill="none" aria-hidden=true flex-shrink=0
              path d="M12 3.5 A8.5 8.5 0 1 1 3.5 12" stroke="theme.color.ink-muted" stroke-width=2.5 stroke-linecap="round"
            column flex=1 min-width=0
              Words(text=loadingText, kind="body", outcome="cancelled", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
          column aria-hidden=true gap="theme.space.xs"
            NavHeadGhost()
            NavGhost(badge=false)
            NavGhost(badge=true)
            NavGhost(badge=false)
          column aria-hidden=true gap="theme.space.xs"
            NavHeadGhost()
            NavGhost(badge=false)
            NavGhost(badge=true)
      else if data == "empty"
        row role="status" background-color="theme.color.surface" border-width="theme.line.width" border-style="solid" border-color="theme.color.line" border-radius="theme.radius.control"
          column flex=1 min-width=0 gap="theme.space.md" padding="theme.space.md"
            Words(text=emptyText, kind="body", outcome="cancelled", level=0, testId=`${testId}-${data}`)
            if emptyLabel != ""
              row
                ActionButton(label=emptyLabel, kind="plain", interaction="idle", outcome="none", press=empty, testId=`${testId}-add`)
      else
        column gap="theme.space.lg"
          for g in groups key=g
            column gap="theme.space.xs"
              if g != ""
                NavHeading(text=g, testId=`${testId}-group-${g}`)
              column gap="theme.space.xs"
                for e in entries.filter(e => e.group == g) key=e.key
                  NavItem(label=e.label, href=e.href, badge=e.badge, current=e.current, marked=(agent == "changed" and e.key == agentKey), note=agentNote, testId=`${testId}-entry-${e.key}`)
      column flex=1 min-height="0"
      if accountName != ""
        row testId=`${testId}-account` align-items="center" gap="theme.space.md" padding-left="theme.space.md" padding-right="theme.space.md" padding-top="theme.space.md" padding-bottom="theme.space.xs" border-top-width="theme.line.width" border-top-style="solid" border-top-color="theme.color.line"
          column width="theme.space.xxl" height="theme.space.xxl" flex-shrink=0 background-color="theme.color.fill" border-radius="theme.radius.pill" align-items="center" justify-content="center" overflow="hidden" aria-hidden=true
            text accountName.trim().slice(0, 1) font="theme.type.label" color="theme.color.ink"
          column flex=1 min-width=0
            text accountName font="theme.type.label" color="theme.color.ink" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
            if accountDetail != ""
              text accountDetail max-width="blocks.nav-role-max" font="theme.type.caption" color="theme.color.ink-muted" white-space="nowrap" overflow="hidden" text-overflow="ellipsis"
